WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:29.980
5248 NVIDIA employees joined a petition past 100,000 names to reinstate Jensen Huang. This is MAG 7 Daily, episode 54. After the board fight, Italy's fine on meta, Apple's China approval, and a private raise that still names NVIDIA and meta, then the counterpoint and a threat on microsoft's mail outage. NVIDIA's board is staring at a later Saturday count from TechCrunch, past 115,000 names. With the petition site listing 5,09,000

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:37.320
165 current employees, 1,108 former employees, and 63,063 shareholders.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:44.680
The information's earlier Saturday tally is the 100,000, and the 5,248 staff, and

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.720
its name's Elon Musk, Epic Games's Tim Sweeney, and Y Combinator's Gary Tan.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.120
TechCrunch adds Repplet Chief Amjad Masad.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:59.000
The tech says Siners think Huang was removed without meaningful due process, asks the board

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.500
to bring him back while an independent investigation sets the facts and says he deserves due process,

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:10.020
not mob justice. He resigned Thursday four days after confessing to an affair with a chip

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:15.700
executive US intelligence suspects of being a Chinese spy, and he has agreed to testify before

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:21.520
Congress. CFO Collette Cress is interim chief while the search for a permanent replacement runs.

00:01:22.603 --> 00:01:26.343
Italy's data protection authority find meta 805 million euros,

00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:32.363
$887 million dollars for opening photos and videos in Android users' galleries without

00:01:32.363 --> 00:01:33.423
explicit consent.

00:01:34.023 --> 00:01:36.683
Bloomberg has the Eurofigure and the dollar conversion.

00:01:37.443 --> 00:01:42.903
Reuters carries the same penalty as $887 million over Android users' data access.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.823
Apple Intelligence has approved for iPad and Mac in China.

00:01:47.383 --> 00:01:50.003
Softonic reports ahead of a December rollout.

00:01:50.563 --> 00:01:54.783
Google's corporate development team has explored buying AI tools that create ads.

00:01:54.783 --> 00:02:00.143
The information reports, and Google is paying start-up high-touch to move advertisers onto

00:02:00.143 --> 00:02:01.523
its customer data tools.

00:02:02.043 --> 00:02:04.163
The point is ads inside AI features.

00:02:04.703 --> 00:02:07.983
After advertisers complain, they cannot see how those ads perform.

00:02:08.723 --> 00:02:13.423
Firm as Grid is planning a $3 billion private raise after its IPO collapsed.

00:02:13.983 --> 00:02:16.983
Bloomberg says, citing the Australian Financial Review.

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:22.563
The plan mixes new equity and debt with prepayments locked in from customers, including

00:02:22.563 --> 00:02:28.443
backer Nvidia and Meta. Google's Gemini glasses now have a starting price of $395.

00:02:29.023 --> 00:02:33.723
The new commercial term after face-hiding limits already set for Gemini on the glasses.

00:02:34.363 --> 00:02:40.983
The sale date is later. Apple has rewritten the clock for iOS 28, Mac OS 28, and the matching

00:02:40.983 --> 00:02:46.743
updates. Mark Gurman reported through Mac rumors. Each yearly release still has three stages.

00:02:46.743 --> 00:02:52.323
Coating inside each stage now runs six weeks instead of four, and convergence shrinks from

00:02:52.323 --> 00:02:56.003
four weeks to two, under new chief executive John Ternis.

00:02:56.603 --> 00:03:01.643
Nvidia's security chief quietly left in August, TechCrunch reports, before Huang stepped

00:03:01.643 --> 00:03:06.563
down over relationships that include an executive at a company suspected of funneling chips to

00:03:06.563 --> 00:03:06.923
China.

00:03:07.363 --> 00:03:11.723
A former intelligence officer told the outlet, this is the sort of leak that travels in

00:03:11.723 --> 00:03:16.403
and ordinary conversation, which most corporate security teams are poorly equipped to catch.

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:19.529
The petition's remedy is putting Hwang back.

00:03:20.109 --> 00:03:24.769
A financial times account says the chip company has only itself to blame for a long list

00:03:24.769 --> 00:03:30.389
of adversaries, and the column tech meme circulated says a post-gentsan Nvidia must reshuffle

00:03:30.389 --> 00:03:35.869
leadership, reset Washington ties, and accept that even the most valuable American company

00:03:35.869 --> 00:03:38.029
cannot dictate American foreign policy.

00:03:38.029 --> 00:03:43.489
On that account, a board vote to restore him does not clear the policy fight those adversaries

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.469
are already using.

00:03:45.364 --> 00:03:50.764
Microsoft and Amazon share a customer fear that showed up in a 30-hour Microsoft 365

00:03:51.214 --> 00:03:56.364
failure, which yesterday was a restored service in which Microsoft now traces to an earlier

00:03:56.364 --> 00:04:00.344
network capacity upgrade that surfaced after a later network change.

00:04:01.084 --> 00:04:06.204
GeekWire from the incident log puts it at about 30 hours and more than 70 countries.

00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:11.284
Tech Explorer puts products offline in at least 74 countries and territories across

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:14.184
the Americas, Europe, Asia, and Africa.

00:04:14.824 --> 00:04:17.824
Outlook, teams, and co-pilot were the services named.

00:04:18.464 --> 00:04:23.924
Microsoft called it technical, not cyber, and not related to AI or agents, and on Saturday

00:04:23.924 --> 00:04:26.444
said the remaining customers and regions were back.

00:04:26.884 --> 00:04:32.704
Charles Lamana, executive vice president for co-pilot, agents, and platform, said cascading

00:04:32.704 --> 00:04:37.584
failures and thundering herds at the network perimeter made recovery harder than normal.

00:04:38.284 --> 00:04:43.904
A thundering herd in his usage is huge numbers of devices reconnecting at once and swamping

00:04:43.904 --> 00:04:45.004
systems as they return.

00:04:45.844 --> 00:04:51.144
Customers were promised a preliminary post-incident report within two business days and a final

00:04:51.144 --> 00:04:56.744
report within five, with a step-by-step timeline and many repair items, and he said Microsoft

00:04:56.744 --> 00:04:58.084
would be very specific.

00:04:58.084 --> 00:05:04.444
The load behind that perimeter is a January figure Microsoft reported, more than 450 million

00:05:04.444 --> 00:05:10.624
paid commercial Microsoft 365 seats, which geek wire reads as roughly one seat for every

00:05:10.624 --> 00:05:11.924
18 people on Earth.

00:05:12.504 --> 00:05:16.464
Unity Health Toronto declared a code gray and said patient care continued.

00:05:17.024 --> 00:05:20.224
Pennsylvania lawmakers went about 18 hours without email.

00:05:20.864 --> 00:05:23.704
A Colorado jail could not take online bond payments.

00:05:23.704 --> 00:05:30.064
business upturn, citing Nikkei, said securities firms and asset managers in Japan fell back on

00:05:30.064 --> 00:05:35.624
facts machines when trade confirmation mail stopped. New York's emergency management office warned

00:05:35.624 --> 00:05:41.544
of delays reaching city agencies. In Singapore, some government systems, including email, were disrupted.

00:05:42.044 --> 00:05:47.364
In London, the UK Supreme Court was not receiving email. It was at least the fourth significant

00:05:47.364 --> 00:05:53.184
outage of this kind this year. A January outage lasted nearly 10 hours. In July, a bug

00:05:53.184 --> 00:05:58.444
an automated network maintenance disrupted Azure and Microsoft 365 for hours.

00:05:59.044 --> 00:06:04.224
On August 31st, an exchange online outage also hit Teams, OneDrive, and SharePoint.

00:06:04.984 --> 00:06:10.084
Geekwire sets that record beside earlier Amazon Web Services incidents, a second cloud

00:06:10.084 --> 00:06:12.604
operator with the same class of customer dependence.

00:06:13.284 --> 00:06:16.004
Friday's FAA ground stop was not part of this.

00:06:16.584 --> 00:06:20.124
Homeland Security Secretary Mark Wayne Mullin said there was no connection.

00:06:20.124 --> 00:06:25.344
information. Microsoft said it had no indication its services were involved, and federal officials

00:06:25.344 --> 00:06:30.984
blamed aging FAA telecom gear. The incident account gives Amazon no role in the upgrade.

00:06:31.584 --> 00:06:36.164
Customers still treat both parameters as one risk, because a network change at either

00:06:36.164 --> 00:06:42.444
can drop mail, chat, and an assistant together, then worsen as devices rush back. Microsoft

00:06:42.444 --> 00:06:48.224
owes the specific repair list Lamanna already promised. Amazon inherits the comparison buyers

00:06:48.224 --> 00:06:50.864
will use the next time its own change window fails.

